1
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:46,406
Thanks for the food.

2
00:01:46,473 --> 00:01:47,874
Thank you so much.

3
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:50,176
NOTICE OF CLOSURE

4
00:01:50,243 --> 00:01:56,082
CLOSING DUE TO ECONOMIC CIRCUMSTANCES.
THANKS FOR 20 YEARS OF SMILES.

5
00:01:56,649 --> 00:01:57,817
How much did you make this month?

6
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,187
Pennies.

7
00:02:01,254 --> 00:02:02,388
And you?

8
00:02:03,756 --> 00:02:04,624
Dead zero.

9
00:02:06,159 --> 00:02:08,595
Do you know what young people earn now?

10
00:02:08,661 --> 00:02:12,565
A median of 2.5 million yen per year,
about 150,000 yen a month after tax.

11
00:02:13,066 --> 00:02:15,602
- No wonder they can't save.
- There's no dream in it.

12
00:02:15,668 --> 00:02:18,505
- None.
- There's no money to steal.

13
00:02:18,571 --> 00:02:21,341
- Here you go.
- Momo!

14
00:02:22,041 --> 00:02:23,276
Are you really closing the shop?

15
00:02:23,343 --> 00:02:25,812
I must get out before I fall into debt.

16
00:02:26,479 --> 00:02:28,815
- Want me to lend you some money?
- Me too.

17
00:02:28,882 --> 00:02:34,354
What are you saying?
You don't have money either.

18
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:37,857
You just drift around with no steady job.
I'll clear these plates.

19
00:02:37,924 --> 00:02:39,592
- Momo!
- Coming.

20
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:45,131
- Should we have told her our real job?
- No way. She would faint from shock.

21
00:02:46,432 --> 00:02:48,735
Another place to relax is disappearing.

22
00:02:48,801 --> 00:02:50,436
We might be next.

23
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:53,640
We're alive, but we are the walking dead.

24
00:02:53,706 --> 00:02:56,910
- You should be fined for your dark poetry!
- It's a life-or-death problem.

25
00:02:56,976 --> 00:02:59,946
No house has money.
There's no money to steal.

26
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:02,048
True. Makes our job a bit pointless.

27
00:03:02,115 --> 00:03:05,885
"Being a thief has meaning too." I bet
normal folks wouldn't want to hear that.

28
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:11,724
We aren't thieves. We are great thieves.
You always say it, Rui.

29
00:03:12,292 --> 00:03:17,430
Thieves are small-time,
going after pennies or groceries.

30
00:03:17,497 --> 00:03:23,102
Meanwhile, great thieves are mysterious,
gallant, and go after treasure!

31
00:03:23,169 --> 00:03:25,071
Then, same goes for great thieves.

32
00:03:25,138 --> 00:03:26,973
Oh, right. Last month...

33
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:32,111
I went to Mr. Kanaizumi's mansion,
the one I used to go to regularly.

34
00:03:32,178 --> 00:03:34,247
- That high-end neighborhood?
- Yes.

35
00:03:34,314 --> 00:03:36,683
For five years,
I've been taking from his savings.

36
00:03:36,749 --> 00:03:38,084
Is that what you call "great"?

37
00:03:39,919 --> 00:03:42,355
I'm just a thief when I have no choice.

38
00:03:42,422 --> 00:03:44,591
Only when I needed cash! Anyway!

39
00:03:44,657 --> 00:03:46,025
Last month, when I went there,

40
00:03:47,427 --> 00:03:48,995
Mr. Kanaizumi was dead.

41
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:55,802
I found him on Wednesday,
and he had died on Monday, so two days.

42
00:03:56,636 --> 00:04:00,073
The next day, Thursday, the housekeepers
would come to clean the bath.

43
00:04:00,139 --> 00:04:02,675
- So I just left him there.
- Oh my.

44
00:04:03,876 --> 00:04:06,012
He really helped me out a lot.

45
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:08,781
So I stayed with him until night.

46
00:04:10,283 --> 00:04:13,219
<i>I don't know if he wanted me there.</i>

47
00:04:16,055 --> 00:04:17,257
<i>That man...</i>

48
00:04:18,257 --> 00:04:20,526
<i>He was probably lonely all his life.</i>

49
00:04:25,231 --> 00:04:26,566
<i>I wish</i>

50
00:04:27,333 --> 00:04:29,636
<i>I had been your friend.</i>

51
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:32,238
<i>I wish I had been your daughter.</i>

52
00:04:35,041 --> 00:04:39,612
"But I'm a thief. Sorry." I thought.

53
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:43,449
And the savings? You took all of it?

54
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:47,954
I felt sad, so I just left the house
without taking anything...

55
00:04:48,021 --> 00:04:49,289
- Are you stupid?
- Yes, I am.

56
00:04:49,355 --> 00:04:52,058
- What a waste.
- Why am I even alive?

57
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:54,160
Hey, a fine for dark poetry.

58
00:04:54,227 --> 00:04:59,666
I wonder if I will ever find
a big treasure, some really big money...

59
00:04:59,732 --> 00:05:02,368
Something that makes my heart race.

60
00:05:02,435 --> 00:05:06,873
<i>In the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office,
there is a big safe.</i>

61
00:05:06,939 --> 00:05:09,075
<i>It's full of money.</i>

62
00:05:09,642 --> 00:05:15,882
<i>It's stuffed with bundles of cash,
and it's always refilled right away.</i>

63
00:05:15,948 --> 00:05:21,054
<i>The Finance Ministry delivers the bundles.
It's the Cabinet's secret stash.</i>

64
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:24,290
<i>Its official name
is the Cabinet Secretariat Reward Funds.</i>

65
00:05:24,357 --> 00:05:28,761
<i>It's used to buy top-secret info,
both at home and abroad.</i>

66
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:31,364
<i>So no receipts are needed,</i>

67
00:05:31,431 --> 00:05:34,534
<i>and they don't have to report
how it was used.</i>

68
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:39,405
<i>So they exploit it and use
the nation's money for their own party!</i>

69
00:05:39,472 --> 00:05:41,708
<i>The nation's money!</i>

70
00:05:41,774 --> 00:05:46,446
<i>It all comes from taxes.
The people's sweat and blood!</i>

71
00:05:46,512 --> 00:05:49,015
<i>Is that even okay?</i>

72
00:05:49,582 --> 00:05:51,818
<i>The system is broken!</i>

73
00:05:54,487 --> 00:05:56,222
I found my treasure!

74
00:05:58,991 --> 00:06:02,829
<i>It's the Seika era,
in the democratic country of Nipponia.</i>

75
00:06:03,563 --> 00:06:06,933
<i>A huge ruling party
has held power for a long time.</i>

76
00:06:07,667 --> 00:06:11,571
<i>This once-rich country
is now on the edge of a cliff.</i>

77
00:06:11,637 --> 00:06:13,806
<i>The gap between rich and poor
keeps growing.</i>

78
00:06:13,873 --> 00:06:16,109
<i>Both blue-collar workers
and yakuza have no money.</i>

79
00:06:16,809 --> 00:06:23,549
<i>In Nagatanicho, the center of this nation,
a great thief has landed.</i>

80
00:06:23,616 --> 00:06:26,052
<i>Her surname is Kisaragi,
her given name is Yayoi.</i>

81
00:06:26,119 --> 00:06:30,323
<i>What she will steal
is the dark money of politicians!</i>

82
00:06:31,190 --> 00:06:32,725
PoliticaLupin!

83
00:06:47,807 --> 00:06:49,509
Don't you find it strange?

84
00:06:49,575 --> 00:06:52,078
Eel is at risk of extinction,

85
00:06:52,145 --> 00:06:54,647
yet there's grilled eel here every day.

86
00:06:54,714 --> 00:06:56,315
What is wrong with this country?

87
00:06:56,382 --> 00:06:59,051
I'll have sushi.
Northern-style seafood bowl.

88
00:07:00,286 --> 00:07:02,255
It's cheaper than eel.

89
00:07:02,321 --> 00:07:05,191
It's not about the price.
Try being more critical.

90
00:07:06,959 --> 00:07:08,428
What do you do every day?

91
00:07:08,995 --> 00:07:10,630
Your sister is worried.

92
00:07:12,231 --> 00:07:14,867
Why not work for me as a secretary?

93
00:07:16,602 --> 00:07:18,337
What, work under you, Masakado?

94
00:07:18,404 --> 00:07:20,406
Call me "Mr. Natsume."
Don't call me by name.

95
00:07:20,473 --> 00:07:22,108
You keep nagging me every day.

96
00:07:22,175 --> 00:07:23,676
You make me say it.

97
00:07:23,743 --> 00:07:24,577
The salary?

98
00:07:24,644 --> 00:07:27,814
A starting private secretary
gets 180,000 yen after tax.

99
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,215
Pretty good.

100
00:07:29,282 --> 00:07:35,021
Good? Back then,
I used to earn 1.5 times this.

101
00:07:36,422 --> 00:07:39,392
<i>- So no receipts are needed...</i>
- She's spouting nonsense again.

102
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:42,128
Someone shut her up.

103
00:07:42,628 --> 00:07:44,864
You can't say stuff like this.

104
00:07:44,931 --> 00:07:45,965
Why say that stuff?

105
00:07:46,032 --> 00:07:48,534
Which TV station thinks this is funny?

106
00:07:48,601 --> 00:07:50,870
No need to go and expose things.

107
00:07:50,937 --> 00:07:54,040
<i>It all comes from taxes.
The people's sweat and blood!</i>

108
00:07:54,106 --> 00:07:56,008
- What a pain.
- Sounds like bad news.

109
00:07:56,909 --> 00:07:58,711
- Will it affect your work?
- A little.

110
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:00,713
Isn't it a scandal?

111
00:08:01,514 --> 00:08:04,584
Not now. Even if that kind of thing
slips out, no one cares.

112
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:05,418
Why?

113
00:08:05,485 --> 00:08:07,353
The media doesn't chase it.

114
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:09,755
If they don't chase it,
there are no follow-ups.

115
00:08:09,822 --> 00:08:12,124
With no follow-ups, people forget.

116
00:08:12,191 --> 00:08:13,793
It will stay on the Internet.

117
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:18,431
Even if it does, most voters
aren't interested in politics.

118
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:21,767
They don't even talk about it,
so it's fine.

119
00:08:34,881 --> 00:08:36,849
Oh, this is cute. Shall we pick this?

120
00:08:37,416 --> 00:08:38,951
- Okay.
- I want this one!

121
00:08:39,018 --> 00:08:40,219
Really? I don't know...

122
00:08:54,133 --> 00:08:55,701
Are you Mr. Paolo?

123
00:08:56,903 --> 00:08:57,803
Here.

124
00:09:01,307 --> 00:09:02,775
- You don't want it?
- I do.

125
00:09:09,982 --> 00:09:11,217
What do you want to know?

126
00:09:11,918 --> 00:09:14,754
Not many companies have cash
to steal from nowadays.

127
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:19,692
I need information from an informant
who knows lots about politics.

128
00:09:19,759 --> 00:09:22,695
I heard from a friend of a friend

129
00:09:23,462 --> 00:09:25,998
that you know such informants.

130
00:09:27,033 --> 00:09:28,501
Do you read newspapers?

131
00:09:29,969 --> 00:09:31,370
Only the local news, sometimes.

132
00:09:31,938 --> 00:09:34,206
- Politics?
- I plan to study it.

133
00:09:35,708 --> 00:09:37,243
What do you plan to do at that level?

134
00:09:37,843 --> 00:09:39,412
I'll steal the Cabinet secret funds.

135
00:09:40,746 --> 00:09:41,647
What?

136
00:09:43,115 --> 00:09:48,754
In the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office,
there is a safe with endless cash in it.

137
00:09:48,821 --> 00:09:51,757
The safe of my dreams.

138
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:55,194
It makes my heart race.

139
00:09:56,262 --> 00:09:58,564
It really motivates me.

140
00:09:59,832 --> 00:10:03,202
You, are you out of your mind?

141
00:10:03,903 --> 00:10:07,106
The office is inside
the Prime Minister's residence,

142
00:10:07,173 --> 00:10:09,775
the second most guarded place in Nipponia.

143
00:10:09,842 --> 00:10:10,676
It's impossible.

144
00:10:11,243 --> 00:10:14,847
I'm actually a genius. Do you know
the conditions that make a genius?

145
00:10:16,549 --> 00:10:19,919
Focus, playfulness, and...

146
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:22,221
a drop of madness.

147
00:10:25,257 --> 00:10:26,993
Do you know any politics-savvy informants?

148
00:10:29,795 --> 00:10:32,865
Who can even enter
the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office?

149
00:10:34,567 --> 00:10:37,670
- Cabinet ministers? Diet members?
- Correct.

150
00:10:37,737 --> 00:10:40,306
If you want to steal money,
become a Diet member.

151
00:10:40,873 --> 00:10:41,707
Listen up.

152
00:10:42,675 --> 00:10:45,211
The House of Representatives
will be dissolved soon.

153
00:10:45,277 --> 00:10:46,545
A general election will begin.

154
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:50,950
Any citizen aged 25 or over can run.

155
00:10:51,784 --> 00:10:55,655
If you win and become a member,
I'll introduce an informant.

156
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:59,725
Female politicians
actually do pretty well.

157
00:10:59,792 --> 00:11:02,928
If you get fans,
you get a lot of support, like an idol.

158
00:11:02,995 --> 00:11:04,497
You're cute too,

159
00:11:05,297 --> 00:11:06,632
so I think you can do it.

160
00:11:18,978 --> 00:11:21,947
- Cheers!
- Cheers.

161
00:11:22,014 --> 00:11:24,050
What? I don't know...

162
00:11:24,116 --> 00:11:25,484
I have small eyes.

163
00:11:25,551 --> 00:11:27,720
I eat too much.

164
00:11:27,787 --> 00:11:29,021
- I get it!
- I wonder...

165
00:11:29,088 --> 00:11:31,123
I think I lack self-confidence?

166
00:11:31,190 --> 00:11:32,024
Yeah...

167
00:11:32,091 --> 00:11:38,297
Hey, those aren't flaws.
They are all your strengths.

168
00:11:38,364 --> 00:11:39,398
- What?
- What?

169
00:11:39,465 --> 00:11:45,871
Small eyes are cool! You can also
change them with makeup. I'm jealous.

170
00:11:45,938 --> 00:11:48,274
- Well, true.
- Eating a lot means you're healthy.

171
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:50,743
You would survive longest
on a deserted island.

172
00:11:50,810 --> 00:11:51,977
I see!

173
00:11:52,044 --> 00:11:55,314
Not having confidence
just means you have room to grow.

174
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:57,049
You're already wonderful,

175
00:11:57,116 --> 00:11:58,918
but with a bit more confidence,

176
00:11:58,984 --> 00:12:00,619
you'll be even better.

177
00:12:00,686 --> 00:12:01,954
You'll only get better.

178
00:12:02,021 --> 00:12:02,955
I see...

179
00:12:03,022 --> 00:12:06,025
All these worries of yours
are because of summer.

180
00:12:06,092 --> 00:12:08,761
Everything is because of summer.

181
00:12:08,828 --> 00:12:10,596
- Because of summer?
- Because of summer?

182
00:12:10,663 --> 00:12:13,032
- Summer's at fault? Why?
- Right?

183
00:12:13,099 --> 00:12:14,934
Yeah, it's summer's fault.

184
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,604
- All right! Here's to summer!
- To summer!

185
00:12:18,671 --> 00:12:19,772
Oh, I have to go.

186
00:12:19,839 --> 00:12:21,340
- Okay.
- Okay.

187
00:12:23,509 --> 00:12:24,677
Should we go already?

188
00:12:25,544 --> 00:12:28,481
- Who is that girl?
- Huh? Isn't she your friend, Yuka?

189
00:12:28,547 --> 00:12:31,851
- I don't know her.
- We're out. One more bottle.

190
00:12:31,917 --> 00:12:34,353
Sorry, I have to go to work now.

191
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:36,288
- I have to go.
- Thanks for the drinks!

192
00:12:36,355 --> 00:12:40,025
- Thanks for the drinks.
- Thank you.

193
00:12:42,194 --> 00:12:43,529
Bye...

194
00:12:52,505 --> 00:12:55,374
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

195
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:56,408
Yay!

196
00:12:59,378 --> 00:13:00,212
Hey.

197
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:02,148
Sorry, I missed the train! How are things?

198
00:13:02,214 --> 00:13:04,617
Perfect. I saved you a spot.

199
00:13:04,683 --> 00:13:05,518
Here.

200
00:13:12,024 --> 00:13:13,359
Sorry I'm late...

201
00:13:17,029 --> 00:13:20,299
My friend called me here. This girl.

202
00:13:23,135 --> 00:13:25,971
- She was here earlier.
- Wait, are you Miyabi?

203
00:13:26,038 --> 00:13:27,840
It's you! Long time no see!

204
00:13:28,407 --> 00:13:31,076
I'm Yayoi. Don't you remember me?

205
00:13:32,444 --> 00:13:35,381
Guess not. You were drunk after all.

206
00:13:37,783 --> 00:13:40,586
<i>Miyabi Kobayakawa, 29, unemployed.</i>

207
00:13:41,287 --> 00:13:44,723
<i>Her mother died of illness,
and she was raised by her grandmother.</i>

208
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:48,294
<i>Her father is Shiro Kobayakawa,
ex-Prime Minister.</i>

209
00:13:49,295 --> 00:13:53,332
<i>He served several terms and is now
vice president of the ruling Kokuji Party.</i>

210
00:13:53,899 --> 00:13:57,469
<i>The Kobayakawas are
a glamorous political family.</i>

211
00:13:58,037 --> 00:14:01,574
<i>But the daughter, Miyabi,
only ever attracts bad rumors.</i>

212
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:05,544
<i>A typical silly rich girl
with too much money and time.</i>

213
00:14:06,278 --> 00:14:09,915
<i>Now, every time she goes out at night,</i>

214
00:14:09,982 --> 00:14:13,886
<i>"bodyguard" watchers follow her
to make sure she doesn't go wild.</i>

215
00:14:13,953 --> 00:14:14,987
<i>Apparently.</i>

216
00:14:15,054 --> 00:14:17,556
Are you one of the hostesses sent here?

217
00:14:17,623 --> 00:14:18,791
Huh?

218
00:14:18,858 --> 00:14:23,829
You can go home. It's boring anyway.
Get your tip from the guard outside.

219
00:14:24,663 --> 00:14:26,599
<i>Heiresses like her
usually have one weakness.</i>

220
00:14:26,665 --> 00:14:28,467
<i>Twisted loneliness.</i>

221
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:33,505
I came here to drink.
What do you want to drink?

222
00:14:33,572 --> 00:14:34,673
Something expensive?

223
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:37,343
Same thing as me? I'll treat you.

224
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:39,345
If you're free, join me.

225
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:42,481
Another bottle, two glasses.

226
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:43,582
Yes, ma'am.

227
00:14:45,317 --> 00:14:46,518
You know the price?

228
00:14:47,386 --> 00:14:49,188
I'm rich, so it's fine.

229
00:14:49,255 --> 00:14:52,625
I'm a great thief.

230
00:14:52,691 --> 00:14:53,659
Huh?

231
00:14:59,398 --> 00:15:03,002
I'm Yayoi "Lupin" Kisaragi!

232
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:11,710
Lupin? Which generation? The Fourth?

233
00:15:11,777 --> 00:15:14,246
- I'm the First.
- So you're a reboot!

234
00:15:16,148 --> 00:15:20,486
Let's drink outside. The weather is nice.
The night wind feels good, you know.

235
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:24,089
- I can't. I have watchers.
- Watchers?

236
00:15:24,723 --> 00:15:28,160
I'm a bad woman, so bad people watch me.

237
00:15:29,695 --> 00:15:33,299
- Yakuza?
- Yes, my yakuza guardians.

238
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:39,071
I'm a girl raised in a box,
so I play inside the box.

239
00:15:39,738 --> 00:15:41,707
In that case...

240
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:45,544
Lupin will steal you away.

241
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:55,654
Ms. Miyabi has collapsed!

242
00:16:00,259 --> 00:16:03,195
- Wow...
- Come on!

243
00:16:33,392 --> 00:16:34,626
YAYOI KISARAGI

244
00:16:35,427 --> 00:16:36,862
BEST BUDS

245
00:16:39,431 --> 00:16:40,599
Huh?

246
00:16:44,803 --> 00:16:46,472
Miyabi Kobayakawa?

247
00:16:47,706 --> 00:16:49,408
<i>Local assembly members of the Kokuji Party</i>

248
00:16:49,475 --> 00:16:53,679
<i>were found to have avoided paying
national health insurance premiums.</i>

249
00:16:53,746 --> 00:16:55,748
<i>They became nominal board members</i>

250
00:16:55,814 --> 00:16:58,917
<i>of an empty
general incorporated association</i>

251
00:16:58,984 --> 00:17:01,653
<i>and set extremely low pay,</i>

252
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:03,822
<i>keeping premiums of over one million yen</i>

253
00:17:03,889 --> 00:17:06,258
<i>down to a few tens of thousands.</i>

254
00:17:06,325 --> 00:17:07,760
<i>About this problem,</i>

255
00:17:07,826 --> 00:17:09,595
<i>Vice President Kobayakawa said...</i>

256
00:17:09,661 --> 00:17:15,601
<i>You say the party did bad things
as an organization,</i>

257
00:17:15,667 --> 00:17:17,469
<i>but it's only a few people.</i>

258
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:20,406
<i>It's an individual problem.</i>

259
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:23,208
<i>The party doesn't need to apologize.</i>

260
00:17:23,275 --> 00:17:26,145
<i>Hours later,
Secretary-General Iwakura said...</i>

261
00:17:26,211 --> 00:17:29,848
We are truly sorry.

262
00:17:29,915 --> 00:17:33,719
<i>The party apologized
for 360 local assembly members</i>

263
00:17:33,786 --> 00:17:36,955
<i>who had avoided insurance premiums.</i>

264
00:17:37,022 --> 00:17:39,525
This makes me look like a fool!

265
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:43,362
The Prime Minister told me to...

266
00:17:44,363 --> 00:17:46,532
Well, he should have told me first.

267
00:17:47,099 --> 00:17:50,235
Before dissolving the House
and calling the election,

268
00:17:50,302 --> 00:17:53,238
we should at least apologize for show.

269
00:17:53,305 --> 00:17:54,907
<i>Will the full facts be revealed?</i>

270
00:17:54,973 --> 00:17:56,308
<i>We're investigating.</i>

271
00:17:56,375 --> 00:17:58,177
<i>Will you just punish four people?</i>

272
00:17:58,744 --> 00:18:00,045
<i>We're investigating.</i>

273
00:18:00,112 --> 00:18:02,514
<i>This was organized illegal activity,
wasn't it?</i>

274
00:18:03,148 --> 00:18:04,583
<i>We're investigating.</i>

275
00:18:04,650 --> 00:18:08,687
<i>Will the members be expelled?
Will you ask them to resign?</i>

276
00:18:09,254 --> 00:18:10,689
<i>We're investigating.</i>

277
00:18:15,227 --> 00:18:16,361
<i>On to the next news.</i>

278
00:18:17,029 --> 00:18:18,997
She didn't even make a joke.

279
00:18:19,898 --> 00:18:21,567
She just accepted it.

280
00:18:22,701 --> 00:18:25,137
Her face and the silence said everything.

281
00:18:26,271 --> 00:18:29,041
- Hayate, enough.
- Yes.

282
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:34,580
Mr. Natsume, please sit.

283
00:18:34,646 --> 00:18:36,415
- You're a Diet member.
- Yeah.

284
00:18:36,482 --> 00:18:38,750
- Don't mind us.
- Thanks.

285
00:18:38,817 --> 00:18:40,385
- All right, then.
- Go ahead.

286
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:43,355
Hayate, you've been secretary
for a year, right?

287
00:18:43,422 --> 00:18:47,860
Yes. I never thought
I would have to run so soon.

288
00:18:47,926 --> 00:18:50,395
I should have watched
my father's elections more closely.

289
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:52,698
Don't worry. It's our home base.

290
00:18:53,432 --> 00:18:55,100
We'll give you a good strategist.

291
00:18:55,167 --> 00:18:57,703
- Thanks.
- Natsume, will you look after him?

292
00:18:59,104 --> 00:18:59,972
You will, right?

293
00:19:00,038 --> 00:19:04,476
Hayate has no election experience.
Natsume is in the Upper House,

294
00:19:05,043 --> 00:19:07,312
so your support would be reassuring.

295
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:09,348
Right?

296
00:19:15,454 --> 00:19:16,889
I would be glad to help.

297
00:19:17,789 --> 00:19:18,724
Thank you.

298
00:19:19,925 --> 00:19:24,863
With our base, plus Hayate's fresh looks
and popularity with women, we can't lose!

299
00:19:24,930 --> 00:19:27,232
Natsume, you have many female fans too.

300
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:30,235
Then should us two form a unit?

301
00:19:30,302 --> 00:19:32,571
Hey now, don't get carried away.

302
00:19:40,546 --> 00:19:42,648
Getting on the daughter's good side

303
00:19:42,714 --> 00:19:44,950
won't get you into the Chief Cabinet
Secretary's Office.

304
00:19:45,617 --> 00:19:48,820
I think she has better chances than me
of becoming a Diet Member.

305
00:19:50,389 --> 00:19:54,393
I looked it up. In Nipponia, nearly 30%
of Diet members are hereditary.

306
00:19:54,459 --> 00:19:56,962
In the Kokuji Party, over 40%.

307
00:19:57,029 --> 00:20:01,133
All of them are second, third,
or fourth generation.

308
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:04,970
Even so, I don't think Miyabi Kobayakawa
can become a Diet Member.

309
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:08,774
Yes?

310
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:10,776
Hey, Miyabi.

311
00:20:12,344 --> 00:20:14,913
Why don't you try running for the Diet?

312
00:20:15,514 --> 00:20:17,316
- A Diet member?
- Yes!

313
00:20:20,152 --> 00:20:23,722
My dad, my grandfather, my uncles,

314
00:20:23,789 --> 00:20:26,425
that uncle over there...
It's full of those guys.

315
00:20:26,491 --> 00:20:28,927
Full of people like them.
It's rotten.

316
00:20:28,994 --> 00:20:31,063
Soon my brother will rot too.

317
00:20:31,830 --> 00:20:33,632
Well, they may be rotten,

318
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:37,102
but you should try joining them too!

319
00:20:37,169 --> 00:20:39,905
Be a Diet Member!

320
00:20:46,445 --> 00:20:48,914
HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES
DISSOLUTION SPEECH

321
00:20:51,316 --> 00:20:54,186
Under Article 7
of the Nipponia Constitution,

322
00:20:54,753 --> 00:20:56,021
the House of Representatives

323
00:20:56,622 --> 00:20:57,990
is hereby dissolved.

324
00:20:58,557 --> 00:21:01,360
<i>Banzai! Banzai!</i>

325
00:21:06,632 --> 00:21:13,105
I can't believe they really dissolved it.

326
00:21:13,171 --> 00:21:15,374
Why would they?

327
00:21:16,341 --> 00:21:19,645
They still have their terms.

328
00:21:19,711 --> 00:21:25,684
Do the full term to the end!
Ninety billion yen!

329
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:32,824
If you have 90 billion to organize
an election, put it into child support!

330
00:21:32,891 --> 00:21:37,095
I can't take this anymore!

331
00:21:39,464 --> 00:21:40,632
Mr. Natsume.

332
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:43,035
I'm right behind you.

333
00:21:47,906 --> 00:21:51,643
I had a feeling you might be,
but I couldn't stop myself.

334
00:21:53,011 --> 00:21:56,048
Good thing you noticed. Please continue.

335
00:22:07,726 --> 00:22:11,330
I heard that
you ran from the bodyguards last night.

336
00:22:11,997 --> 00:22:13,999
Mr. Shiro was angry.

337
00:22:14,066 --> 00:22:16,234
I'll try not to run into him.

338
00:22:16,301 --> 00:22:18,537
He's quite busy with the election.

339
00:22:18,603 --> 00:22:20,205
Another election?

340
00:22:27,846 --> 00:22:28,847
What?

341
00:22:29,581 --> 00:22:32,150
<i>You're serious? I'll fully support you.</i>

342
00:22:33,652 --> 00:22:36,788
- What are you saying?
<i>- The video. Check your Winstagram.</i>

343
00:22:37,356 --> 00:22:39,224
<i>I've been waiting for this day.</i>

344
00:22:39,291 --> 00:22:41,493
- Sorry, I'm hanging up.
<i>- Huh?</i>

345
00:22:46,732 --> 00:22:49,568
<i>I will become a Diet Member!</i>

346
00:22:50,135 --> 00:22:50,969
What?

347
00:22:51,670 --> 00:22:53,438
<i>I am running in this election!</i>

348
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:56,241
<i>Everything is because of summer!</i>

349
00:23:05,617 --> 00:23:06,985
YAYOI
I GOT THE DOCUMENTS

350
00:23:12,824 --> 00:23:14,059
ELECTION APPLICATION FORM

351
00:23:14,126 --> 00:23:15,527
No way...

352
00:23:32,844 --> 00:23:33,945
She's fast.

353
00:23:38,683 --> 00:23:40,952
My Winsta. What was that?
What is going on?

354
00:23:42,854 --> 00:23:43,889
You don't remember?

355
00:23:45,090 --> 00:23:46,057
What?

356
00:23:46,725 --> 00:23:47,559
Huh?!

357
00:23:47,626 --> 00:23:50,028
Have you ever thought
of becoming a politician?

358
00:23:50,695 --> 00:23:52,798
Well, I have.

359
00:23:52,864 --> 00:23:54,032
What?

360
00:23:54,099 --> 00:23:56,835
I come from a political family.
Of course I was interested.

361
00:23:56,902 --> 00:23:59,004
It was my dream in middle school.

362
00:23:59,070 --> 00:24:04,376
- Then...
- They don't want female politicians.

363
00:24:04,443 --> 00:24:07,512
- There are many women now though.
- Not many.

364
00:24:08,613 --> 00:24:11,783
Women are only 14%
of the House of Representatives.

365
00:24:11,850 --> 00:24:17,122
Out of 180 countries,
we rank 140th for the share of women.

366
00:24:17,189 --> 00:24:18,023
Really.

367
00:24:18,089 --> 00:24:20,659
See? They don't want us.

368
00:24:20,725 --> 00:24:23,395
- I want you.
- To steal the money for her.

369
00:24:23,462 --> 00:24:25,430
- What did you say?
- Miyabi.

370
00:24:26,097 --> 00:24:28,867
Life is short. Stand up, young lady!

371
00:24:28,934 --> 00:24:31,736
- It's "Fall in love, young lady."
- This is no time for love!

372
00:24:31,803 --> 00:24:35,607
We will live.
We'll survive in this Nipponia.

373
00:24:35,674 --> 00:24:38,210
- Survive, young lady?
- Shout out loud, young lady!

374
00:24:38,276 --> 00:24:39,511
What should I shout?

375
00:24:39,578 --> 00:24:41,980
"I will become a Diet member!"

376
00:24:42,047 --> 00:24:43,615
- Huh?
- Here!

377
00:24:43,682 --> 00:24:45,684
- Huh?
- Repeat! Okay!

378
00:24:47,752 --> 00:24:50,689
I will become a Diet member!

379
00:24:52,190 --> 00:24:54,059
<i>I am running in this election!</i>

380
00:24:54,125 --> 00:24:57,729
<i>Everything is because of summer!</i>

381
00:25:01,967 --> 00:25:05,136
Perfect. That was a nice shout.

382
00:25:05,203 --> 00:25:08,740
- You two are just drunk.
- Saying it out loud is important.

383
00:25:08,807 --> 00:25:11,710
So we won't forget it tomorrow.
Let's start here.

384
00:25:11,776 --> 00:25:15,380
- Let's post this on my Winsta.
- What?

385
00:25:16,014 --> 00:25:18,884
What? Wait! Don't touch social media
when you're drunk.

386
00:25:18,950 --> 00:25:20,852
I'm not drunk.

387
00:25:22,621 --> 00:25:25,023
Yay! It's summer's fault!

388
00:25:26,391 --> 00:25:28,593
It's summer's fault. It's summer's fault.

389
00:25:30,762 --> 00:25:33,932
- It's fine. Why not do it for real?
- No, never.

390
00:25:34,699 --> 00:25:38,403
I work as a consultant.
It's my first election, but I can help.

391
00:25:38,470 --> 00:25:41,406
- Wait...
- You posted it on Winsta.

392
00:25:41,473 --> 00:25:42,908
I deleted it.

393
00:25:42,974 --> 00:25:44,643
Don't you know deleting things
makes it spread?

394
00:25:44,709 --> 00:25:46,711
No one will take it seriously.

395
00:25:47,445 --> 00:25:50,815
"That silly girl is saying silly things
again." They'll laugh at me.

396
00:25:51,683 --> 00:25:53,151
That's not true...

397
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:54,619
It is like that for me.

398
00:25:55,387 --> 00:25:57,155
It has always been like that.

399
00:25:57,722 --> 00:25:58,557
Jeez.

400
00:25:59,391 --> 00:26:01,927
It's better I don't try anything.

401
00:26:06,364 --> 00:26:10,001
My childhood dream was to be a thief.

402
00:26:10,936 --> 00:26:13,305
A great thief who travels the world.

403
00:26:14,139 --> 00:26:15,040
There it is.

404
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:18,710
Yep. People laughed at me too, like that.

405
00:26:20,979 --> 00:26:22,714
But I was serious.

406
00:26:26,151 --> 00:26:27,886
I wanted to become a great thief

407
00:26:28,787 --> 00:26:30,522
and give money to everyone.

408
00:26:31,790 --> 00:26:33,592
So that the people I love

409
00:26:33,658 --> 00:26:36,828
would live life with a little more ease.

410
00:26:39,764 --> 00:26:40,932
So they could live

411
00:26:41,733 --> 00:26:42,834
happily.

412
00:26:44,202 --> 00:26:47,505
So they could feel glad to be alive.

413
00:26:59,184 --> 00:27:00,452
What I said last night,

414
00:27:01,152 --> 00:27:02,654
I meant that.

415
00:27:05,156 --> 00:27:06,358
I will

416
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:08,727
steal you.

417
00:27:13,064 --> 00:27:14,799
Away from the cramped box

418
00:27:15,767 --> 00:27:17,535
that confines you.

419
00:27:22,841 --> 00:27:24,009
Do you want to get out?

420
00:27:25,043 --> 00:27:26,011
Or not?

421
00:27:29,014 --> 00:27:30,115
What do you want?

422
00:27:38,556 --> 00:27:39,658
What?

423
00:27:39,724 --> 00:27:41,793
<i>Miyabi is running.</i>

424
00:27:42,427 --> 00:27:43,628
<i>In the general election.</i>

425
00:27:43,695 --> 00:27:45,030
ELECTION APPLICATION FORM

426
00:27:47,198 --> 00:27:48,533
<i>You'll help, right?</i>

427
00:27:49,434 --> 00:27:50,502
Why me?

428
00:27:50,568 --> 00:27:54,105
<i>You are that informant who is savvy
about politics, right?</i>

429
00:27:56,408 --> 00:27:58,076
Together, we can steal...

430
00:27:59,010 --> 00:28:00,412
those politicians' money.

431
00:28:08,053 --> 00:28:09,754
Stealing politics...

432
00:28:11,289 --> 00:28:13,191
That could be fun.

433
00:28:17,962 --> 00:28:20,331
My name is Inui.

434
00:28:34,112 --> 00:28:36,181
NIPPONIA ELECTION
CANDIDATES SURVEY

435
00:28:36,247 --> 00:28:39,517
Tanaka, Miyamoto,

436
00:28:40,585 --> 00:28:41,920
and Hayate...

437
00:28:41,986 --> 00:28:45,090
Let's put them on the priority list.

438
00:28:45,857 --> 00:28:48,626
You said we would win easily.

439
00:28:49,961 --> 00:28:53,998
If Mr. Shiro's son happens to lose,
it will be a disaster.

440
00:28:55,533 --> 00:28:57,535
Who do you propose we cut?

441
00:28:58,970 --> 00:29:01,906
- Natsume...
- If you add people, you have to cut.

442
00:29:03,108 --> 00:29:06,177
The headwind against us is blowing hard.

443
00:29:06,244 --> 00:29:09,647
- We can't lose a single seat now.
- With all due respect...

444
00:29:10,415 --> 00:29:12,150
We are over budget.

445
00:29:13,151 --> 00:29:15,553
You can't keep acting like a bureaucrat.

446
00:29:17,055 --> 00:29:19,257
If we lose this election,
everything is meaningless.

447
00:29:20,191 --> 00:29:21,192
We are...

448
00:29:23,695 --> 00:29:24,829
over budget.

449
00:29:29,801 --> 00:29:33,138
Well, let's respect our Finance Director.

450
00:29:34,239 --> 00:29:36,040
<i>It would be sad to hurt his motivation.</i>

451
00:29:36,875 --> 00:29:38,042
Oh, right.

452
00:29:39,110 --> 00:29:41,146
Let's take it out of that safe.

453
00:29:41,780 --> 00:29:43,882
I'll tell my younger brother.

454
00:29:47,218 --> 00:29:50,121
- Call the Cabinet Secretary for support.
- Roger.

455
00:29:51,089 --> 00:29:52,557
Starting next week,

456
00:29:52,624 --> 00:29:54,859
things will get busy.

457
00:29:57,562 --> 00:29:59,697
What? Here?

458
00:29:59,764 --> 00:30:01,099
It's a hideout.

459
00:30:02,333 --> 00:30:03,334
ORIENT HALL

460
00:30:03,401 --> 00:30:07,405
Inui has supported many politicians.
He's amazing.

461
00:30:07,472 --> 00:30:13,044
Like Shin Sakuma, or Yoshiaki Ishizuka.
Inui was behind all of their successes.

462
00:30:13,111 --> 00:30:17,615
But none of them will say they know Inui.

463
00:30:17,682 --> 00:30:19,984
After all, that remains a secret.

464
00:30:20,652 --> 00:30:22,754
Don't tell anyone about Inui.

465
00:30:22,821 --> 00:30:23,988
That's the condition.

466
00:30:24,589 --> 00:30:25,423
Understood.

467
00:30:26,291 --> 00:30:28,993
Well, he is not...

468
00:30:29,561 --> 00:30:31,196
a shady person at all.

469
00:30:31,262 --> 00:30:34,365
He's just an ordinary old man.
Don't worry.

470
00:30:35,133 --> 00:30:39,103
Oh, welcome! Come on!

471
00:30:41,139 --> 00:30:42,707
See? Don't worry.

472
00:30:46,811 --> 00:30:49,347
- Did you write it?
- Yes.

473
00:30:55,687 --> 00:30:56,888
Excuse me.

474
00:31:01,793 --> 00:31:04,863
Mr. Inui, you're an election pro, right?

475
00:31:04,929 --> 00:31:05,730
What?

476
00:31:06,764 --> 00:31:07,599
Yeah.

477
00:31:08,233 --> 00:31:11,169
I am basically an information broker
who knows politics.

478
00:31:12,570 --> 00:31:13,471
And?

479
00:31:13,538 --> 00:31:16,107
- I know elections too.
- Okay.

480
00:31:18,309 --> 00:31:20,678
Do you think I can win?

481
00:31:21,312 --> 00:31:24,449
I'm from a political family,
but I have nothing.

482
00:31:24,515 --> 00:31:26,551
I'm 29 and unemployed.

483
00:31:26,618 --> 00:31:27,752
That's hard.

484
00:31:29,420 --> 00:31:33,925
A naive, rich girl with no backing
sweeping up votes?

485
00:31:33,992 --> 00:31:35,560
The world isn't a fairy tale.

486
00:31:36,961 --> 00:31:37,795
However...

487
00:31:38,763 --> 00:31:40,131
There's a way.

488
00:31:57,148 --> 00:32:00,051
- Normally I leave it to my secretary.
- Thank you.

489
00:32:00,685 --> 00:32:02,186
All experience is good.

490
00:32:02,820 --> 00:32:07,191
People from political families like me
are always called out of touch.

491
00:32:08,860 --> 00:32:11,062
- Sorry to make you join me.
- It's fine.

492
00:32:12,063 --> 00:32:13,298
Oh no!

493
00:32:15,099 --> 00:32:16,100
Miyabi?

494
00:32:17,869 --> 00:32:19,771
Miyabi? What are you doing?!

495
00:32:19,837 --> 00:32:22,440
Oh, wrong person. Excuse me.

496
00:32:24,309 --> 00:32:25,777
- Excuse me.
- Excuse me.

497
00:32:26,577 --> 00:32:27,545
Excuse me.

498
00:32:33,251 --> 00:32:34,886
You're running for election?

499
00:32:35,520 --> 00:32:36,454
You?

500
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:45,563
- Is that the shape of Chiba District 2?
- Huh?

501
00:32:46,397 --> 00:32:48,666
District 2 is my father's electoral zone.
Our home is there.

502
00:32:48,733 --> 00:32:51,035
- You have a house outside Tokyo?
- Yeah.

503
00:32:51,636 --> 00:32:55,006
No one lives in it now, but our residence
is still registered there.

504
00:32:55,073 --> 00:32:57,675
If we register in Tokyo,
people will be upset.

505
00:32:57,742 --> 00:33:01,646
That's the base of the Kobayakawa kingdom.

506
00:33:01,713 --> 00:33:02,580
DISTRICT 2

507
00:33:02,647 --> 00:33:04,182
Do you know the vote-value gap?

508
00:33:05,750 --> 00:33:09,020
The number of residents
differs by district.

509
00:33:09,721 --> 00:33:11,689
Because of population changes,

510
00:33:11,756 --> 00:33:14,058
the value of one vote differs by region.

511
00:33:14,125 --> 00:33:14,926
Correct.

512
00:33:15,493 --> 00:33:20,431
To correct this inequality, which relates
to Article 14 of the Constitution,

513
00:33:20,498 --> 00:33:23,935
districts are redrawn regularly
based on the census.

514
00:33:24,002 --> 00:33:26,137
This time was no exception.

515
00:33:26,971 --> 00:33:29,140
So, a new district was created.

516
00:33:32,343 --> 00:33:36,614
District 17. The eldest Kobayakawa son,
Hayate, will run here.

517
00:33:37,815 --> 00:33:40,485
Father in District 2,
Hayate in District 17.

518
00:33:40,551 --> 00:33:43,154
The plan is for them to win both.

519
00:33:44,355 --> 00:33:46,024
We'll put the daughter

520
00:33:46,858 --> 00:33:48,459
of the Kobayakawa family in District 17.

521
00:33:48,526 --> 00:33:49,394
What?

522
00:33:54,499 --> 00:33:55,867
Chiba District 17.

523
00:33:55,933 --> 00:33:58,569
Huh? The same as me?

524
00:33:59,971 --> 00:34:02,907
Does Mr. Shiro know about this?

525
00:34:07,545 --> 00:34:09,547
I don't think he'll allow it.

526
00:34:09,614 --> 00:34:15,186
Running is a citizen's right. Don't you
know it, Mr. Masakado Natsume?

527
00:34:16,154 --> 00:34:20,358
<i>Masakado Natsume, 45.
Upper House member of the Kokuji Party.</i>

528
00:34:20,425 --> 00:34:21,893
<i>A former Finance Ministry official.</i>

529
00:34:21,959 --> 00:34:24,395
<i>In his second term
since entering politics.</i>

530
00:34:24,462 --> 00:34:26,264
Oh, Mr. Natsume!

531
00:34:26,864 --> 00:34:28,299
- Mr. Natsume!
- Mr. Natsume!

532
00:34:28,366 --> 00:34:30,601
<i>His serious-looking attractiveness
gained him many fans.</i>

533
00:34:32,437 --> 00:34:34,338
Politicians aren't idols.

534
00:34:35,072 --> 00:34:37,275
NATSUME
I TRUST IN YOU

535
00:34:37,341 --> 00:34:40,678
<i>He used to belong to no faction.</i>

536
00:34:40,745 --> 00:34:42,580
<i>But after factions broke up two years ago,</i>

537
00:34:42,647 --> 00:34:45,650
<i>he got close to the leaders
of the old Kobayakawa faction.</i>

538
00:34:45,716 --> 00:34:47,585
<i>He was chosen as Finance Director.</i>

539
00:34:47,652 --> 00:34:50,488
<i>Meaning, he's the party's treasurer.</i>

540
00:34:51,055 --> 00:34:54,492
<i>So he's close to the Cabinet secret funds.</i>

541
00:34:55,660 --> 00:34:59,330
<i>As for his weakness,
there are rumors about his relationships.</i>

542
00:35:00,965 --> 00:35:04,068
<i>He rarely refuses a date, but...</i>

543
00:35:04,135 --> 00:35:05,603
This is delicious.

544
00:35:07,138 --> 00:35:08,773
Is it?

545
00:35:10,975 --> 00:35:15,746
My mother's chicken-and-egg rice bowl
is much better.

546
00:35:18,282 --> 00:35:20,952
<i>As a total mama's boy,
he gets dumped right away.</i>

547
00:35:21,652 --> 00:35:25,356
<i>But some suspect
he behaves like that on purpose.</i>

548
00:35:25,423 --> 00:35:26,724
<i>The truth is unknown.</i>

549
00:35:27,625 --> 00:35:30,895
<i>At least, he's the type
who does not act coldly toward women.</i>

550
00:35:33,197 --> 00:35:36,734
- Who are you?
- I'm Yayoi. Miyabi's friend.

551
00:35:36,801 --> 00:35:39,036
What kind of friend?

552
00:35:39,103 --> 00:35:40,304
Are you perhaps...

553
00:35:41,172 --> 00:35:42,807
interested in me?

554
00:35:43,975 --> 00:35:44,909
Yes, I am.

555
00:35:46,911 --> 00:35:50,314
Oh, I'm happy.

556
00:36:09,534 --> 00:36:10,368
Sir!

557
00:36:11,068 --> 00:36:12,069
Sir!

558
00:36:12,136 --> 00:36:14,005
You're so noisy.

559
00:36:14,071 --> 00:36:15,640
Miyabi is running!

560
00:36:16,207 --> 00:36:17,275
Which horse is that?

561
00:36:18,209 --> 00:36:20,478
I'm talking about your daughter!

562
00:36:21,979 --> 00:36:24,515
She applied
for screening at party headquarters.

563
00:36:25,683 --> 00:36:28,486
She'll run in Chiba District 17.

564
00:36:33,591 --> 00:36:35,426
No matter what you've done,

565
00:36:35,993 --> 00:36:38,829
even when you troubled our family,
I always forgave you.

566
00:36:38,896 --> 00:36:40,097
What is your complaint?

567
00:36:41,098 --> 00:36:43,234
Causing trouble for your brother...

568
00:36:44,569 --> 00:36:46,504
Is it fun for you? Huh?

569
00:36:47,972 --> 00:36:49,674
Is someone tricking you?

570
00:36:50,241 --> 00:36:54,812
- Did some opposition party tempt you?
- No. I'm independent.

571
00:36:54,879 --> 00:36:56,047
Miyabi.

572
00:36:56,113 --> 00:36:58,683
We are a special family.

573
00:37:00,251 --> 00:37:02,053
A priceless, beautiful,

574
00:37:02,820 --> 00:37:04,155
red diamond.

575
00:37:05,056 --> 00:37:08,659
Many people want to get their hands
on such a jewel.

576
00:37:08,726 --> 00:37:10,962
I've told you since you were small.

577
00:37:11,796 --> 00:37:13,297
Don't let yourself get used.

578
00:37:14,599 --> 00:37:17,168
Become someone who uses people.

579
00:37:20,304 --> 00:37:21,706
What about you, brother?

580
00:37:22,273 --> 00:37:24,342
Aren't you being used by Dad?

581
00:37:25,209 --> 00:37:27,979
By the family pressure
to become a politician?

582
00:37:28,045 --> 00:37:30,781
You used to say you wanted
to create games.

583
00:37:31,916 --> 00:37:32,984
I was a kid.

584
00:37:33,050 --> 00:37:35,820
Then you joined
our uncle's construction firm.

585
00:37:35,886 --> 00:37:37,488
Because Dad told you to.

586
00:37:37,555 --> 00:37:39,624
Then you quit to become his secretary.

587
00:37:39,690 --> 00:37:42,526
And now you're running.
Because Dad said so, right?

588
00:37:43,594 --> 00:37:47,265
What will you do as a politician, brother?
What do you want to do?

589
00:37:52,370 --> 00:37:53,437
Well...

590
00:37:55,006 --> 00:37:58,009
- I will influence the country...
- How?

591
00:37:58,843 --> 00:38:00,745
Then what do you want to do?

592
00:38:07,952 --> 00:38:09,754
If I become a politician,

593
00:38:09,820 --> 00:38:11,822
I'll end the inheritance of seats.

594
00:38:14,492 --> 00:38:16,260
I'll reform the election system.

595
00:38:17,762 --> 00:38:18,663
What?

596
00:38:19,563 --> 00:38:20,965
How foolish.

597
00:38:38,115 --> 00:38:39,450
What are you doing?

598
00:38:40,584 --> 00:38:43,254
I need cash.

599
00:38:43,321 --> 00:38:46,957
- You can't do that.
- No one will know if we stay quiet.

600
00:38:48,726 --> 00:38:50,895
- Sir!
- Leave her alone.

601
00:38:51,862 --> 00:38:53,264
She will learn soon enough.

602
00:38:56,267 --> 00:38:59,403
Real politics aren't
like a simulation game.

603
00:39:01,072 --> 00:39:04,008
HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES

604
00:39:04,875 --> 00:39:06,043
Mr. Natsume.

605
00:39:07,778 --> 00:39:09,647
Tell me about District 17.

606
00:39:09,714 --> 00:39:12,683
Hmm, I can't say anything.

607
00:39:12,750 --> 00:39:14,018
Don't be like that.

608
00:39:15,519 --> 00:39:16,654
I'll just say this.

609
00:39:17,555 --> 00:39:20,391
Miyabi can run if she wants,
but she can't win.

610
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:30,868
Excuse me.

611
00:39:31,435 --> 00:39:34,372
CHIEF CABINET SECRETARY OFFICE

612
00:39:35,473 --> 00:39:36,440
Yes.

613
00:39:36,507 --> 00:39:39,443
SECRETARY
MATSUKICHI TAKENOKOSHI

614
00:39:41,545 --> 00:39:43,981
REQUESTED THE BELOW SUM
FOR 8 REWARD PAYMENTS

615
00:39:44,048 --> 00:39:46,484
100 MILLION YEN

616
00:39:47,251 --> 00:39:48,953
- Take care of it.
- Yes.

617
00:40:07,238 --> 00:40:10,841
<i>In the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office,
there is a big safe.</i>

618
00:40:13,077 --> 00:40:15,379
<i>It's full of money.</i>

619
00:40:17,982 --> 00:40:21,185
<i>It's stuffed with bundles of cash.</i>

620
00:40:22,820 --> 00:40:25,256
<i>It's the Cabinet's secret stash.</i>

621
00:40:25,322 --> 00:40:28,692
<i>Its official name
is the Cabinet Secretariat Reward Funds.</i>

622
00:40:28,759 --> 00:40:33,197
<i>It's used to buy top-secret info,
both at home and abroad.</i>

623
00:40:33,264 --> 00:40:36,066
<i>So no receipts are needed,</i>

624
00:40:36,967 --> 00:40:40,638
<i>and they don't have to report
how it was used.</i>

625
00:40:41,372 --> 00:40:45,943
<i>So they exploit it and use
the nation's money for their own party!</i>

626
00:40:46,010 --> 00:40:47,978
<i>The nation's money!</i>

627
00:40:48,579 --> 00:40:53,217
<i>It all comes from taxes.
The people's sweat and blood!</i>

628
00:40:53,284 --> 00:40:56,086
<i>Is that even okay?</i>

629
00:40:56,153 --> 00:40:58,823
<i>The system is broken!</i>

630
00:40:59,857 --> 00:41:02,860
Elections are about base,
signboard, and bag.

631
00:41:02,927 --> 00:41:05,629
Signboard is how much fame you got.
The bag is money.

632
00:41:05,696 --> 00:41:07,031
Campaign funds.

633
00:41:07,898 --> 00:41:11,735
Public support is great and all,
but you need cash too.

634
00:41:12,870 --> 00:41:16,073
First, you must set up a support group,
or no money moves.

635
00:41:16,140 --> 00:41:18,576
Deposit is three million.

636
00:41:18,642 --> 00:41:22,179
You need three million yen just to run?
How expensive!

637
00:41:22,246 --> 00:41:25,583
It's not just three million.
Everything costs money.

638
00:41:25,649 --> 00:41:29,887
Office rent, staff pay, campaign car,
signs and banners,

639
00:41:29,954 --> 00:41:33,491
social media, online ads,
flyers and newspaper ads,

640
00:41:33,557 --> 00:41:35,993
team jackets, lunches,
expenses and extras.

641
00:41:36,060 --> 00:41:37,495
About 20 million in total!

642
00:41:40,030 --> 00:41:43,000
The more money,
the higher the chance of winning.

643
00:41:43,067 --> 00:41:46,537
Even before the start date,
the battle has already begun.

644
00:41:48,506 --> 00:41:49,673
Let me hear it.

645
00:41:53,511 --> 00:41:55,212
This is our seasonal greeting.

646
00:41:56,614 --> 00:41:58,749
Our seasonal greeting.

647
00:41:59,683 --> 00:42:01,452
Our seasonal greeting.

648
00:42:02,553 --> 00:42:05,122
Our seasonal greeting.

649
00:42:05,189 --> 00:42:07,358
Thank you very much.

650
00:42:16,500 --> 00:42:17,368
He's here.

651
00:42:17,434 --> 00:42:21,438
- Mr. Hayate, look over here!
- Smile, please!

652
00:42:21,505 --> 00:42:23,140
That's Miyabi, his sister!

653
00:42:25,509 --> 00:42:28,245
Wow. You're like a celebrity.

654
00:42:28,312 --> 00:42:29,647
My parents are.

655
00:42:36,053 --> 00:42:37,688
- Thank you.
- Yes.

656
00:42:37,755 --> 00:42:38,989
I'll check it.

657
00:42:41,125 --> 00:42:42,393
Excuse me...

658
00:42:43,394 --> 00:42:45,729
Oh, me? I'm Miyabi's friend.

659
00:42:47,998 --> 00:42:49,400
Another "friend."

660
00:42:50,234 --> 00:42:51,402
One more poster.

661
00:42:51,468 --> 00:42:53,404
This should be it.

662
00:42:54,271 --> 00:42:55,639
- Here?
- Okay.

663
00:42:58,042 --> 00:43:00,744
- Let's call it a day. Thank you.
- Thank you.

664
00:43:09,620 --> 00:43:13,357
- Who's this?
- Miyabi's real friend, Kaoru Sera.

665
00:43:14,458 --> 00:43:15,759
Did you tell them you're a thief?

666
00:43:15,826 --> 00:43:17,261
Of course not.

667
00:43:17,928 --> 00:43:21,899
My cover is a consultant who wants
to have more female politicians.

668
00:43:21,966 --> 00:43:24,835
Miyabi thinks the thief talk is a joke.

669
00:43:25,903 --> 00:43:26,904
You're a sly woman.

670
00:43:26,971 --> 00:43:29,807
A sly great thief.

671
00:43:31,542 --> 00:43:33,644
The road to the Cabinet Secretary's safe...

672
00:43:34,545 --> 00:43:35,980
is still long.

673
00:43:38,882 --> 00:43:40,217
Until then,

674
00:43:42,386 --> 00:43:45,489
I'll take Nagatanicho's money.

675
00:43:48,659 --> 00:43:51,195
It's all treasure.

676
00:44:01,672 --> 00:44:04,274
<i>Next episode! Chiba District 17,
the battlefield of the election.</i>

677
00:44:04,341 --> 00:44:08,746
<i>Hayate, the thoroughbred from a good
family, against the wild horse, Miyabi.</i>

678
00:44:08,812 --> 00:44:10,581
<i>Will the brother win, or the sister?</i>

679
00:44:10,648 --> 00:44:14,151
<i>A battle between siblings turns
sacred elections into a hellish scene!</i>

680
00:44:14,218 --> 00:44:16,720
- Don't say "puke."
- You brought it up first.

681
00:44:16,787 --> 00:44:18,122
No, I didn't say "puke."

682
00:44:18,188 --> 00:44:19,223
You just did.

683
00:44:19,289 --> 00:44:21,792
<i>Will Nipponia be okay?
Hang in there, Nipponia.</i>

684
00:44:21,859 --> 00:44:24,695
<i>The great thief takes her first step,
sneaking into the world!</i>

685
00:44:24,762 --> 00:44:26,597
<i>The game of deception begins!</i>

686
00:44:26,664 --> 00:44:28,932
We should thank the great thief.

687
00:44:28,999 --> 00:44:29,900
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
